volumes-e2e-*.json: /run/thimsy/volumes.json exactly as thimsy-session wrote it during its own E2E
run (linux/src/thimsy-session/tests/e2e/test_e2e.py, unchanged, against the sanitized session
binary; G7-volumes). A wrapper replaced only the test's volumes() reader so that every distinct text
it read was saved, in order:

  00-boot             at start: the empty list
  01-coldplug         the second card's FAT drive, 1234-ABCD, mounted
  02-games-checking   the boot card's exFAT games drive, 9602-C755, being checked
  03-games-mounted    9602-C755 mounted (boot_disk)
  04-ejected          1234-ABCD after an eject request
  05-pulled           the boot card pulled: 9602-C755 gone

volumes_test.cpp parses each one and answers from them. If the session's writer changes
(VolumeManager::toJson, linux/docs/session.md), capture these again the same way.
